{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-h24v-f482-8cwf","published":"2026-11-12T18:18:44Z","modified":"2026-11-12T18:30:04.026467930Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-84974"],"summary":"code16/sharp: Arbitrary class instantiation through the embed_key API parameter","details":"### Impact\n\nAn authenticated attacker can instantiate any class in the PHP application by using the `embed_key` parameter across multiple API endpoints. The instantiation is performed by the Laravel container. As a result, the `__construct()` method of the class is called and all constructor dependencies are resolved. The attacker cannot specify parameter values and cannot call any arbitrary method.\n\n### Patches\n\nThe problem has been patched in 9.23.0 and pre-release version 10.0.0-beta.4. An additional check was added to verify that `embed_key` is a class extending `SharpFormEditorEmbed` before any instantiation.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNo known workarounds.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"code16/sharp","ecosystem":"Packagist","purl":"pkg:composer/code16/sharp"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.23.0"}]}],"versions":["7.0.0-alpha.1","7.27.0","7.7.2","v4.0-BETA1","v4.0-BETA2","v4.0-BETA3","v4.0-BETA4","v4.0-BETA5","v4.0-BETA6","v4.0.0","v4.0.1","v4.0.10","v4.0.11","v4.0.12","v4.0.13","v4.0.14","v4.0.15","v4.0.16","v4.0.17","v4.0.18","v4.0.19","v4.0.2","v4.0.20","v4.0.21","v4.0.3","v4.0.4","v4.0.5","v4.0.6","v4.0.7","v4.0.8","v4.0.9","v4.1.0","v4.1.1","v4.1.10","v4.1.11","v4.1.12","v4.1.13","v4.1.14","v4.1.15","v4.1.16","v4.1.17","v4.1.18","v4.1.19","v4.1.2","v4.1.20","v4.1.21","v4.1.22","v4.1.23","v4.1.24","v4.1.25","v4.1.3","v4.1.4","v4.1.5","v4.1.6","v4.1.7","v4.1.8","v4.1.9","v4.2.0","v4.2.1","v4.2.2","v4.2.3","v4.2.4","v4.2.5","v4.2.6","v5.0.0","v5.0.0-alpha.1","v5.0.0-alpha.10","v5.0.0-alpha.2","v5.0.0-alpha.3","v5.0.0-alpha.4","v5.0.0-alpha.5","v5.0.0-alpha.6","v5.0.0-alpha.7","v5.0.0-alpha.8","v5.0.0-alpha.9","v5.0.1","v5.1.0","v5.1.1","v5.1.2","v5.2.0","v5.3